{
 "title": "A Volume-Price-Adjusted MACD Trading Strategy with Sensitivity Calibration for U.S. Equity Indices",
 "hypothesis": "H0: mu_new <= mu_old vs Ha: mu_new > mu_old (one-sided 5% level) for Pair1 B vs A, Pair2 C vs A, Pair3 C vs B",
 "data_sources": [
  "Yahoo Finance daily OHLCV for SPY, QQQ, DIA"
 ],
 "sample": "Daily OHLCV data for 3 US equity indices traded as ETFs: S&P 500 (SPY), NASDAQ-100 (QQQ), Dow Jones Industrial Average (DIA) from Yahoo Finance. Sample spans 2018 to February 2026. Weekends and non-trading days excluded. Training period 2018-2022: 1,259 trading days per instrument used for calibration of lambda. Testing period 2023-01-01 to 2026-02-28: 791 trading days per instrument used for out-of-sample evaluation. No leverage. Long-only, fully invested on buy signal with minimum 1 share, exit on sell signal, wait for next buy. Execution at opening price next trading day to avoid look-ahead bias. Transaction cost 4 bps one-way (3 bps trading +1 bp slippage), 8 bps round-trip. Three strategies evaluated: A Baseline MACD (12,26,9), B MACD+lambda with index-specific optimal lambda, C VP-MACD with index-specific optimal lambda.",
 "period_start": "2018",
 "period_end": "February 2026",
 "method": [
  "1. Data: Yahoo Finance daily Open, High, Low, Close, Volume for SPY/QQQ/DIA; exclude non-trading days.",
  "2. Traditional MACD: EMA_t = alpha*P_t + (1-alpha)*EMA_{t-1} with alpha = 2/(n+1), n=12 fast, n=26 slow; MACD_t = EMA12(P_t) - EMA26(P_t); Signal_t = EMA9(MACD_t); Histogram = MACD_t - Signal_t.",
  "3. Baseline trading rule (Strategy A): Buy if MACD_{t-1} <= Signal_{t-1} and MACD_t > Signal_t; Sell if MACD_{t-1} >= Signal_{t-1} and MACD_t < Signal_t; also zero-line rule defined but not used for evaluation.",
  "4. Volume-price-adjusted price P*_t = sum_{i=t-N}^{t-1} P_i*Volume_i*sigma_i*r_i / sum_{i=t-N}^{t-1} Volume_i where N is rolling window (not stated), P_i is Close, sigma_i = STD(High_i - Low_i)/Close_i, r_i = |Close_i - Open_i|/(High_i - Low_i).",
  "5. VP-MACD_t = EMA12(P*_t) - EMA26(P*_t); Signal_t = EMA9(VP-MACD_t) (Eq.5-6).",
  "6. Lambda-adjusted entry (Strategies B,C): Buy if VP-MACD_{t-1} <= lambda*Signal_{t-1} and VP-MACD_t > lambda*Signal_t; Sell if VP-MACD_{t-1} >= Signal_{t-1} and VP-MACD_t < Signal_t; lambda in (0.8,1); lambda<1 lowers threshold for earlier entry.",
  "7. Backtest setup: initial capital $100,000; long-only, fully invested on buy, closed on sell; min 1 share; leverage none; execution at next trading day open; costs 4 bps one-way (3 bps trade +1 bp slippage), 8 bps round-trip applied at entry and exit.",
  "8. Calibration: grid search lambda in [0.8,1.0] step 0.02 (11 values) separately for MACD+lambda and VP-MACD per index on training 2018-2022 (1,259 days). Selection via multi-criteria on win ratio, total PnL, PnL ratio, Sharpe, max drawdown, expectancy; primary criterion Sharpe ratio (Table 1). Selected lambdas fixed for testing: MACD+lambda SPY 0.90, QQQ 0.84, DIA 0.92; VP-MACD SPY 0.88, QQQ 0.98, DIA 0.86.",
  "9. Evaluation on testing 2023-01-01 to 2026-02-28 (791 days per instrument): Total Trades N (buy-sell pair =1 trade), Win Ratio = N_win/N, PnL Ratio = (Gains/N_win)/(Losses/N_loss), Expectancy = WinRatio*avgGain - (1-WinRatio)*avgLoss, Total PnL = V_T - V_0, Sharpe = mean(R_t)/sd(R_t)*sqrt(252), MDD = max_t (Peak_t - Value_t)/Peak_t where Peak_t = max_{s<=t} Value_s.",
  "10. Statistical tests on daily return differences in testing period: one-sided t-test H0: mu_new <= mu_old vs Ha: mu_new > mu_old for 3 pairwise comparisons (Pair1 B vs A, Pair2 C vs A, Pair3 C vs B) per index; Newey-West HAC t-test with adjusted SEs (lags/bandwidth not stated); circular block bootstrap with 1,000 resamples, block length 5 consecutive daily returns, p-values reported for significant cases."
 ],
